# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities. What makes the route interesting is a single idea, taken from the *flow set* framework of Gandon et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the work that also motivated the [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") in this package:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini membangun circuit untuk **dinamika waktu model Fermi-Hubbard satu dimensi**, mulai dari menuliskan Hamiltonian sampai memeriksa densitas site hasil evolusi. Yang membuat jalur ini menarik adalah satu ide dari framework *flow set* oleh Gandon dkk. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), karya yang juga melatarbelakangi [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") di paket ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Instead of grouping Hamiltonian terms *after* the fermion-to-qubit mapping, group them *before* it, into **flow sets**, one-dimensional subsets of the directed fermionic interaction graph whose transfer operators mutually commute.\n"
msgstr "> Alih-alih mengelompokkan suku Hamiltonian *setelah* pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit, kelompokkan *sebelum* pemetaan, ke dalam **flow set**, yaitu himpunan bagian satu dimensi dari graf interaksi fermionik berarah yang operator transfernya saling komut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That choice drives everything below. It calls for the following:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan itu menentukan semua yang ada di bawah. Ini membutuhkan hal-hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom fermion-to-qubit encoding** tailored to the flow sets, which here spends one **ancilla qubit** so the qubit count associated with the implementation of a given Hamiltonian term no longer grows with the number of fermionic modes (as is the case for Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"
msgstr "**Encoding fermion-ke-qubit kustom** yang disesuaikan dengan flow set, yang di sini memakai satu **qubit ancilla** sehingga jumlah qubit yang terkait dengan implementasi suku Hamiltonian tertentu tidak lagi bertambah seiring jumlah mode fermionik (seperti pada Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom synthesis** that exploits the commutativity within each set. The payoff is a circuit whose two-qubit depth is **constant in the system size**, against the linear growth of a JW-based term-by-term Trotterization.\n"
msgstr "**Synthesis kustom** yang memanfaatkan sifat komutatif di dalam tiap set. Hasilnya adalah circuit dengan depth dua-qubit yang **konstan terhadap ukuran sistem**, dibandingkan pertumbuhan linear pada Trotterisasi suku-per-suku berbasis JW.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The machinery that gets an encoding of your own into the transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) carries over to any model.\n"
msgstr "Mekanisme yang memasukkan encoding buatanmu sendiri ke transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) berlaku untuk model apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout, and the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the general recipe for writing a custom mapper.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Lihat juga\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [Panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) untuk stage transpiler yang dirujuk di seluruh panduan ini, dan [panduan mapper](mappers#mappers-explanation) untuk resep umum menulis mapper kustom.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transfer operators and flow sets {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"
msgstr "Operator transfer dan flow set {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") is built from vertex operators $V_j$ and transfer operators $T_{jk}$. In terms of fermionic creation and annihilation operators,\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") dibangun dari operator vertex $V_j$ dan operator transfer $T_{jk}$. Dalam bentuk operator kreasi dan anihilasi fermionik,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so $V_j$ measures the occupation of mode $j$ (it is $+1$ when empty and $-1$ when filled), while $T_{jk}$ transfers a fermion along the *directed* edge $j \\to k$. Note that the two indices of $T_{jk}$ are *not* interchangeable. The first index carries the minus combination and the second carries the plus, which is what makes $T_{jk}$ distinct from $T_{kj}$ and gives the edge its orientation.\n"
msgstr "jadi $V_j$ mengukur okupansi mode $j$ (bernilai $+1$ saat kosong dan $-1$ saat terisi), sedangkan $T_{jk}$ memindahkan sebuah fermion sepanjang edge *berarah* $j \\to k$. Perhatikan bahwa kedua indeks pada $T_{jk}$ *tidak* bisa dipertukarkan. Indeks pertama membawa kombinasi minus dan indeks kedua membawa plus, dan inilah yang membuat $T_{jk}$ berbeda dari $T_{kj}$ serta memberi edge arahnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These satisfy *mixed* commutation relations. Two transfer operators acting on **disjoint** sites commute trivially, since each is an *even* product of fermionic operators. The interesting case is a shared site. There, the two **commute** if the arrows *flow* through that site (one arrives, one leaves) and **anticommute** if they *clash* (both arrive, or both leave).\n"
msgstr "Keduanya memenuhi relasi komutasi *campuran*. Dua operator transfer yang bekerja pada site yang **tidak saling beririsan** komut secara trivial, karena masing-masing adalah hasil kali *genap* operator fermionik. Kasus yang menarik adalah site yang dipakai bersama. Di sana, keduanya **komut** jika panahnya *mengalir* melalui site itu (satu datang, satu pergi) dan **antikomut** jika *bertabrakan* (keduanya datang, atau keduanya pergi).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rule is easiest to see on a picture. Drawing the vertices as nodes and each $T_{jk}$ as an arrow from $j$ to $k$ gives the *directed* interaction graph, here for the four-site chain used throughout this guide, which carries both orientations of every bond:\n"
msgstr "Aturan ini paling mudah dilihat lewat gambar. Menggambar vertex sebagai node dan tiap $T_{jk}$ sebagai panah dari $j$ ke $k$ menghasilkan graf interaksi *berarah*, di sini untuk rantai empat site yang dipakai di seluruh panduan ini, yang membawa kedua orientasi untuk setiap ikatan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace the rule on the figure. Look at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{2,3}$, for example. One arrow *arrives* at site 2 and the other *leaves* it, so the fermion flows straight through and the two operators commute. Look instead at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{3,2}$. Both arrows *point into* site 2. They clash, and those two anticommute.\n"
msgstr "Telusuri aturannya pada gambar. Lihat $T_{1,2}$ dan $T_{2,3}$, misalnya. Satu panah *tiba* di site 2 dan yang lain *pergi* darinya, jadi fermion mengalir lurus melewatinya dan kedua operator komut. Sekarang lihat $T_{1,2}$ dan $T_{3,2}$. Kedua panah *menunjuk ke* site 2. Mereka bertabrakan, dan keduanya antikomut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is what makes flow sets possible. Pick a set of arrows forming a directed path and every pair either meets head-to-tail or does not meet at all, so the whole set commutes, even though the individual operators overlap on shared sites. Evolving under a single flow set therefore incurs **no Trotter error**, and as [step 7](#flowsets-synthesis) shows, it can also be done at constant circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Inilah yang memungkinkan flow set. Pilih sekumpulan panah yang membentuk jalur berarah, dan setiap pasangan entah bertemu kepala-ke-ekor atau tidak bertemu sama sekali, sehingga seluruh set komut, meskipun operator individualnya beririsan di site bersama. Karena itu, evolusi di bawah satu flow set tidak menimbulkan **error Trotter**, dan seperti ditunjukkan [langkah 7](#flowsets-synthesis), ini juga bisa dilakukan dengan depth circuit yang konstan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian Fermi-Hubbard {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D Fermi-Hubbard model on $L$ sites (spinless, open boundaries) is\n"
msgstr "Model Fermi-Hubbard 1D pada $L$ site (tanpa spin, batas terbuka) adalah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following Eq. (9) of Ref. <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the hopping term is $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. The interaction is diagonal, so it is expressed through vertex operators using $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"
msgstr "Mengikuti Pers. (9) dari Ref. <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), suku hopping-nya adalah $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. Interaksinya diagonal, jadi dinyatakan lewat operator vertex dengan $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both pieces are built directly as a [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Note that $V_j$ is stored as the diagonal entry `(j, j)`:\n"
msgstr "Kedua bagian dibangun langsung sebagai [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Perhatikan bahwa $V_j$ disimpan sebagai entri diagonal `(j, j)`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interior sites pick up a coefficient of $-1$ on $V_j$ because they appear in two bonds, whereas the boundary sites only appear in one. Every term listed here appears in the graph drawn above. The `T(j,k)` terms are its arrows, and the `V(j)` terms its nodes.\n"
msgstr "Site interior mendapat koefisien $-1$ pada $V_j$ karena muncul di dua ikatan, sedangkan site tepi hanya muncul di satu. Setiap suku yang tercantum di sini muncul di graf yang digambar di atas. Suku `T(j,k)` adalah panahnya, dan suku `V(j)` adalah node-nya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"partition-into-flow-sets\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Partition into flow sets {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"
msgstr "2. Partisi ke dalam flow set {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, label each term with the flow set it belongs to. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute exists for this purpose. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per group ([step 6](#flowsets-transpile) puts this to work), so the grouping decided here at the *fermionic* level survives into the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, beri label pada tiap suku dengan flow set tempatnya berada. Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") ada untuk tujuan ini. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") atas operator yang dikelompokkan terdekomposisi menjadi satu [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per grup ([langkah 6](#flowsets-transpile) memanfaatkan ini), sehingga pengelompokan yang diputuskan di sini pada level *fermionik* bertahan sampai ke circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the 1D chain, the two hopping flow sets are the east-oriented arrows ($T_{j,j+1}$) and the west-oriented arrows ($T_{j+1,j}$). The diagonal interaction terms commute with everything diagonal and form a third group:\n"
msgstr "Untuk rantai 1D, dua flow set hopping adalah panah berorientasi timur ($T_{j,j+1}$) dan panah berorientasi barat ($T_{j+1,j}$). Suku interaksi diagonal komut dengan semua yang diagonal dan membentuk grup ketiga:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups 0 and 1 are the two flow sets. Each set is a directed path along the chain, so by the flow property all terms within a group commute.\n"
msgstr "Grup 0 dan 1 adalah dua flow set. Tiap set adalah jalur berarah sepanjang rantai, jadi berdasarkan sifat flow semua suku dalam satu grup komut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group also has to be Hermitian on its own, since a product formula exponentiates the groups separately and only a Hermitian factor has a unitary evolution. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") confirms it:\n"
msgstr "Tiap grup juga harus Hermitian dengan sendirinya, karena product formula mengeksponensiasi grup secara terpisah dan hanya faktor Hermitian yang punya evolusi uniter. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") mengonfirmasinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is worth pausing on, because the two hopping groups are *one-directional*: group 0 holds only east-oriented terms and group 1 only west-oriented ones. Splitting a Hamiltonian that way would normally break Hermiticity, since $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ needs its conjugate partner $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ alongside it. A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") avoids the problem because $T_{jk}$ is *already* Hermitian on its own. It is a product of two Majorana operators (see its definition in step 1), not a bare $a^\\dagger_j a_k$, so its Jordan-Wigner image carries a real coefficient rather than an imaginary one. Choosing this operator representation is therefore what makes a one-directional flow set a legitimate Trotter factor at all.\n"
msgstr "Ini patut dicermati, karena dua grup hopping bersifat *satu arah*: grup 0 hanya berisi suku berorientasi timur dan grup 1 hanya yang berorientasi barat. Memecah Hamiltonian seperti itu biasanya merusak sifat Hermitian, karena $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ membutuhkan pasangan konjugatnya $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ di sampingnya. [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") menghindari masalah ini karena $T_{jk}$ *sudah* Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Ia adalah hasil kali dua operator Majorana (lihat definisinya di langkah 1), bukan $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ polos, sehingga citra Jordan-Wigner-nya membawa koefisien real, bukan imajiner. Memilih representasi operator ini karena itu yang membuat flow set satu arah menjadi faktor Trotter yang sah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The east/west labels used throughout this guide are **geometric**, with the chain drawn left to right and mode indices increasing in that direction; $T_{j,j+1}$ points east and $T_{j+1,j}$ points west. Ref.   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) is internally inconsistent on this naming (its prose and its figures disagree) so this guide deliberately does *not* follow the prose, and instead keeps the labels from the picture. When cross-reading with the paper, match the flow sets by their Pauli weights (1 and 3 below), not by the compass words.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Label timur/barat yang dipakai di seluruh panduan ini bersifat **geometris**, dengan rantai digambar dari kiri ke kanan dan indeks mode bertambah ke arah itu; $T_{j,j+1}$ menunjuk ke timur dan $T_{j+1,j}$ menunjuk ke barat. Ref.   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) tidak konsisten secara internal soal penamaan ini (teks dan gambarnya tidak sejalan), jadi panduan ini sengaja *tidak* mengikuti teksnya, dan sebagai gantinya mempertahankan label dari gambar. Saat membaca silang dengan makalah, cocokkan flow set berdasarkan bobot Pauli-nya (1 dan 3 di bawah), bukan berdasarkan kata arah mata angin.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

