#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"write-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Write the custom encoding {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Tulis encoding kustom {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Section IV B of Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) classifies the forms that a local fermion-to-qubit encoding can take when restricted to a flow set. Plain Jordan-Wigner uses $N_q = N_f$ qubits and maps every hopping term to a weight-2 Pauli. The classification shows that **spending extra qubits buys structure** in the encoded operators.\n"
msgstr "Bagian IV B dari Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) mengklasifikasikan bentuk yang bisa diambil encoding fermion-ke-qubit lokal ketika dibatasi pada sebuah flow set. Jordan-Wigner biasa memakai $N_q = N_f$ qubit dan memetakan setiap suku hopping ke Pauli berbobot 2. Klasifikasi itu menunjukkan bahwa **mengeluarkan qubit tambahan membeli struktur** pada operator yang di-encode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding implemented here is the parity-delocalized construction of Appendix B 2 (equations B4 and B5), which uses one **ancilla qubit**, so $N_q = N_f + 1$. The fermionic parity is delocalized across a pair of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Encoding yang diimplementasikan di sini adalah konstruksi parity-delocalized dari Appendix B 2 (persamaan B4 dan B5), yang memakai satu **qubit ancilla**, jadi $N_q = N_f + 1$. Paritas fermionik didelokalisasi di sepasang qubit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The index $j+2$ in the last expression forces the extra qubit. The chain’s final bond has $j = N_f - 2$, so its $Z_{j+2}$ lands on qubit $N_f$, one past the last fermionic mode $N_f - 1$. That trailing qubit is the ancilla, and it is why $N_q = N_f + 1$ rather than $N_f$. The same reach shows up in $V_j$, whose $Z_{j+1}$ is on the ancilla for $j = N_f - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Indeks $j+2$ pada ekspresi terakhir memaksa adanya qubit tambahan. Ikatan terakhir rantai punya $j = N_f - 2$, jadi $Z_{j+2}$-nya jatuh pada qubit $N_f$, satu melewati mode fermionik terakhir $N_f - 1$. Qubit di ujung itulah ancilla, dan itulah sebabnya $N_q = N_f + 1$, bukan $N_f$. Jangkauan yang sama muncul pada $V_j$, yang $Z_{j+1}$-nya berada di ancilla untuk $j = N_f - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is visible immediately; one whole flow set is mapped to a sum of weight-1 Paulis.\n"
msgstr "Keuntungannya langsung terlihat; satu flow set utuh dipetakan menjadi jumlah Pauli berbobot 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ prefactors are fixed by the normalization $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, and the relative minus sign between the two orientations is fixed by the product identity $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, which the Paulis above satisfy. Getting either wrong yields an operator that obeys the commutation relations but no longer represents the same Hamiltonian, so you should verify the encoding numerically, as shown in [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Prefaktor $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ ditentukan oleh normalisasi $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, dan tanda minus relatif antara kedua orientasi ditentukan oleh identitas hasil kali $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, yang dipenuhi oleh Pauli di atas. Salah di salah satunya menghasilkan operator yang mematuhi relasi komutasi tetapi tidak lagi merepresentasikan Hamiltonian yang sama, jadi kamu sebaiknya memverifikasi encoding secara numerik, seperti ditunjukkan di [langkah 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing the encoding means writing a function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") handles the iteration over terms and their composition:\n"
msgstr "Menulis encoding berarti menulis fungsi yang memetakan satu operator transfer umum ke sebuah string Pauli; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") menangani iterasi atas suku dan komposisinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") expects the signature `(operator, num_qubits)`, and the return type must be a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which makes the function directly usable as a transpiler plugin. See [step 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") mengharapkan signature `(operator, num_qubits)`, dan tipe kembaliannya harus berupa [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), sehingga fungsi itu bisa langsung dipakai sebagai plugin transpiler. Lihat [langkah 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying it to the Hamiltonian from step 1 gives the encoded operator on $N_f + 1 = 5$ qubits:\n"
msgstr "Menerapkannya pada Hamiltonian dari langkah 1 menghasilkan operator ter-encode pada $N_f + 1 = 5$ qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are 14 terms, in three shapes: the hopping has become `X` and `ZXZ`, the interaction `ZZ`, and the leading `[]` is the identity, contributing only a global phase. Note that the `ZZ` terms reach nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors; $V_jV_{j+1}$ spans qubits $j$ through $j+2$, which is the cost of delocalizing the parity.\n"
msgstr "Ada 14 suku, dalam tiga bentuk: hopping menjadi `X` dan `ZXZ`, interaksi menjadi `ZZ`, dan `[]` di awal adalah identitas, yang hanya menyumbang fase global. Perhatikan bahwa suku `ZZ` menjangkau tetangga terdekat *dan* tetangga terdekat berikutnya; $V_jV_{j+1}$ membentang dari qubit $j$ sampai $j+2$, yang merupakan harga dari mendelokalisasi paritas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grouping by flow set exposes the asymmetry the construction buys. List the Pauli weights present in each group:\n"
msgstr "Mengelompokkan berdasarkan flow set memperlihatkan asimetri yang dibeli oleh konstruksi ini. Daftarkan bobot Pauli yang ada di tiap grup:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The east-oriented flow set (group 0) consists **entirely of weight-1 Paulis**. Its time evolution is therefore a layer of single-qubit rotations and needs *no entangling gates*, whereas under Jordan-Wigner every hopping term is weight-2 and requires them. This is the space-time trade-off of Ref. <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) in its simplest form: one extra qubit converts half of the hopping Hamiltonian into single-qubit rotations.\n"
msgstr "Flow set berorientasi timur (grup 0) terdiri **seluruhnya dari Pauli berbobot 1**. Evolusi waktunya karena itu berupa satu lapis rotasi single-qubit dan *tidak membutuhkan gate entangling*, sedangkan di bawah Jordan-Wigner setiap suku hopping berbobot 2 dan membutuhkannya. Inilah trade-off ruang-waktu dari Ref. <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) dalam bentuk paling sederhana: satu qubit tambahan mengubah separuh Hamiltonian hopping menjadi rotasi single-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The west-oriented flow set (group 1) pays for it at weight three, and the interaction (group 2) sits at weight two, where the weight-zero entry is the identity. None of this is yet a *circuit* claim; what a synthesis makes of these weights is the subject of steps 6 and 7.\n"
msgstr "Flow set berorientasi barat (grup 1) membayarnya di bobot tiga, dan interaksi (grup 2) berada di bobot dua, di mana entri berbobot nol adalah identitas. Semua ini belum merupakan klaim tentang *circuit*; apa yang dihasilkan synthesis dari bobot-bobot ini adalah topik langkah 6 dan 7.\n"

