#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Verify the encoding {#4-verify-the-encoding}"
msgstr "4. Verifikasi encoding {#4-verify-the-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A custom encoding is only useful if it is *faithful*, and a hand-written one should be checked. Because this encoding uses $N_f + 1$ qubits, the qubit Hilbert space is twice as large as the fermionic one, so the encoded Hamiltonian cannot equal the Jordan-Wigner one term by term. The two are related by an isometry instead.\n"
msgstr "Encoding kustom hanya berguna jika *setia* (faithful), dan encoding yang ditulis tangan sebaiknya diperiksa. Karena encoding ini memakai $N_f + 1$ qubit, ruang Hilbert qubit dua kali lebih besar daripada ruang fermionik, sehingga Hamiltonian ter-encode tidak bisa sama dengan Hamiltonian Jordan-Wigner suku demi suku. Keduanya dihubungkan oleh sebuah isometri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Where the isometry comes from:** Under Jordan-Wigner a basis state is the occupation string; qubit $j$ holds $n_j$. This encoding instead stores *cumulative parities*. Define\n"
msgstr "**Asal isometri:** Di bawah Jordan-Wigner, sebuah basis state adalah string okupansi; qubit $j$ menyimpan $n_j$. Encoding ini sebaliknya menyimpan *paritas kumulatif*. Definisikan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so bit $b_{j+1}$ records the parity of all occupations up to and including site $j$. There are $N_f + 1$ such bits for $N_f$ occupations, which is where the ancilla comes from. The occupation is recovered as the *difference* between neighboring bits, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. An occupied site therefore shows up as a **domain wall** between two adjacent bits, which is why this is called a domain-wall (or Kramers-Wannier) encoding. That is also why $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: the product of two neighboring $Z$s reads off that difference.\n"
msgstr "jadi bit $b_{j+1}$ mencatat paritas semua okupansi sampai dan termasuk site $j$. Ada $N_f + 1$ bit seperti itu untuk $N_f$ okupansi, dan dari situlah ancilla berasal. Okupansi dipulihkan sebagai *selisih* antara bit bertetangga, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. Site yang terisi karena itu muncul sebagai **domain wall** di antara dua bit yang berdampingan, makanya disebut encoding domain-wall (atau Kramers-Wannier). Itu juga sebabnya $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: hasil kali dua $Z$ bertetangga membaca selisih tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing this map out for a few states makes the structure concrete (note that $b_0 = 0$ is fixed, so only half of the $2^{N_f+1}$ qubit states are in the image, and hence an isometry rather than a unitary):\n"
msgstr "Dengan menuliskan peta ini untuk beberapa state, strukturnya jadi lebih jelas (perhatikan bahwa $b_0 = 0$ itu tetap, jadi hanya setengah dari $2^{N_f+1}$ state qubit yang ada di image, dan karena itu berupa isometri, bukan unitari):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single fermion on site 0 flips every cumulative parity above it, which is the delocalization at work. Collecting these columns into a matrix gives the isometry $W$, and the encoding is faithful when it *intertwines* the two Hamiltonians:\n"
msgstr "Satu fermion di site 0 membalik setiap paritas kumulatif di atasnya, dan inilah delokalisasi yang bekerja. Kalau kolom-kolom ini dikumpulkan jadi satu matriks, kita dapat isometri $W$, dan encoding-nya dikatakan faithful kalau ia *mengaitkan* (intertwine) kedua Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, mapping a fermionic state into the qubit space and then evolving it there must give the same result as evolving it in the fermionic space first and mapping afterward.\n"
msgstr "Artinya, memetakan state fermionik ke ruang qubit lalu mengevolusikannya di sana harus memberi hasil yang sama dengan mengevolusikannya lebih dulu di ruang fermionik lalu memetakannya sesudahnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The intertwining relation holds exactly, and separately for each flow set. That second, stronger statement is what later steps rely on: a product formula evolves the groups one at a time, and a product of intertwined factors is itself intertwined, so any *approximation* built from these groups agrees between the two encodings even though the encodings differ. As a corollary, the spectra must agree, with every Jordan-Wigner eigenvalue appearing twice in the larger space, once for each value of the unconstrained global parity:\n"
msgstr "Relasi intertwining ini berlaku persis, dan berlaku terpisah untuk tiap flow set. Pernyataan kedua yang lebih kuat itulah yang dipakai langkah-langkah berikutnya: product formula mengevolusikan grup satu per satu, dan hasil kali faktor-faktor yang intertwined itu sendiri juga intertwined, jadi *aproksimasi* apa pun yang dibangun dari grup-grup ini akan sama di antara kedua encoding, meski encoding-nya berbeda. Sebagai akibatnya, spektrumnya harus sama, dengan setiap eigenvalue Jordan-Wigner muncul dua kali di ruang yang lebih besar, sekali untuk tiap nilai paritas global yang tidak dibatasi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-build\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Build the fermionic circuit {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "5. Bangun fermionic circuit {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before involving any qubits, the dynamics are expressed on the *fermionic* level. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") acts on fermionic modes rather than qubits, and an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over the Hamiltonian is the whole circuit:\n"
msgstr "Sebelum melibatkan qubit apa pun, dinamikanya dinyatakan di level *fermionik*. Sebuah [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") bekerja pada mode fermionik, bukan qubit, dan sebuah gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") atas Hamiltonian itu sudah menjadi seluruh circuit-nya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one opaque box over all four modes, and the interesting part is what it decomposes into. The `synthesis` argument says how: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the first-order product formula, which splits the operator by its [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") and evolves each group in turn. So the flow-set partitioning from step 2 *is* the Trotterization, and a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) performs it, giving **one** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **per flow set** in group order: east, west, then the diagonal interaction, carrying 3, 3, and 8 terms respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ada satu kotak buram untuk keempat mode, dan bagian menariknya adalah apa yang diuraikan darinya. Argumen `synthesis` menentukan caranya: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") adalah product formula orde pertama, yang memecah operator berdasarkan [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\")-nya dan mengevolusikan tiap grup secara bergantian. Jadi partisi flow set dari langkah 2 *adalah* Trotterisasinya, dan satu panggilan [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) langsung melakukannya, menghasilkan **satu** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **per flow set** sesuai urutan grup: east, west, lalu interaksi diagonal, masing-masing membawa 3, 3, dan 8 suku.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this happens entirely in fermionic space: no qubit has been mentioned yet, and the approximation is already made. The number of Trotter steps therefore belongs here too, as [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), which divides the time and repeats the whole sweep:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa semua ini terjadi sepenuhnya di ruang fermionik: belum ada qubit yang disebut, dan aproksimasinya sudah dibuat. Jumlah langkah Trotter karena itu juga ada di sini, sebagai [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), yang membagi waktu dan mengulang seluruh sapuan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nine gates: the three flow sets, cycled through three times at a third of the time each. That cycling is what makes it a Trotterization rather than a re-slicing of one group. Repeating a *single* group would achieve nothing, since consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` is just `A(t)`. A formula that reads the groups can interleave them; one applied after the mapping cannot, because the grouping is gone by then.\n"
msgstr "Sembilan gate: tiga flow set, diputar tiga kali dengan sepertiga waktu untuk masing-masing. Perputaran itulah yang menjadikannya Trotterisasi, bukan sekadar memotong ulang satu grup. Mengulang satu grup *saja* tidak akan memberi apa-apa, karena eksponensial berurutan dari operator yang sama saling komut, jadi `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` sama saja dengan `A(t)`. Formula yang membaca grup bisa menyisipkannya bergantian; formula yang diterapkan setelah pemetaan tidak bisa, karena pengelompokannya sudah hilang saat itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the step that makes the grouping matter. Each emitted gate is mapped and synthesized independently, so everything downstream acts on the partitioning decided at the fermionic level. Skipping the decomposition hands the whole operator to the next stage instead, and the grouping is ignored.\n"
msgstr "Inilah langkah yang membuat pengelompokan jadi penting. Setiap gate yang dihasilkan dipetakan dan disintesis secara independen, jadi semua yang ada di hilir bekerja berdasarkan partisi yang diputuskan di level fermionik. Kalau dekomposisi dilewati, seluruh operator diserahkan begitu saja ke tahap berikutnya, dan pengelompokannya diabaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Transpile with the custom encoding {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "6. Transpile dengan encoding kustom {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is now ready to be used by the transpiler. Two more pieces are needed:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang encoding-nya siap dipakai oleh transpiler. Dua bagian lagi dibutuhkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A layout.** The default [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") assumes one qubit per mode, which is wrong in this situation. [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") associates the fermionic register with a [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) of a different size, which is how ancilla qubits enter the pipeline.\n"
msgstr "**Sebuah layout.** [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") yang default mengasumsikan satu qubit per mode, dan itu keliru untuk kasus ini. [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") mengaitkan register fermionik dengan sebuah [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) berukuran berbeda, dan lewat cara inilah qubit ancilla masuk ke pipeline.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A synthesis plugin.** [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes the mapper function directly, maps the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate’s Hamiltonian with it, and emits a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), preserving the $e^{-itH}$ convention. Its [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\") decides how that gate is turned into rotations. Note that this is a *second*, independent product formula, acting on qubits after the mapping: Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) is passed here, and step 7 replaces it with one that knows about flow sets.\n"
msgstr "**Sebuah synthesis plugin.** [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") menerima fungsi mapper secara langsung, memetakan Hamiltonian dari gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") dengannya, lalu menghasilkan sebuah [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), dengan konvensi $e^{-itH}$ tetap terjaga. [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")-nya menentukan bagaimana gate itu diubah menjadi rotasi. Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah product formula *kedua* yang independen, bekerja pada qubit setelah pemetaan: [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) milik Qiskit dipakai di sini, dan langkah 7 menggantinya dengan yang paham flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since every comparison below reruns this pipeline, it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Karena setiap perbandingan di bawah menjalankan ulang pipeline ini, ada baiknya dibungkus sekali saja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four fermionic modes have become a five-qubit circuit, with the ancilla supplied by the custom layout.\n"
msgstr "Empat mode fermionik telah menjadi circuit lima qubit, dengan ancilla yang disediakan oleh layout kustom.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now look at what the resulting circuit actually contains. Decomposing repeatedly reduces the evolution gates all the way down to `U` and `CX`, so that the two-qubit cost of the two synthesis strategies compared below is measured in the same currency: [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) then reports the `CX` count, and [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) takes a filter function to measure the two-qubit depth. Note that this `reps` is a decomposition depth, unrelated to the number of Trotter steps a product formula takes, which also goes by `reps` later in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang lihat apa isi circuit hasilnya. Dekomposisi berulang menurunkan gate evolusi sampai ke `U` dan `CX`, sehingga biaya dua-qubit dari kedua strategi sintesis yang dibandingkan di bawah terukur dengan satuan yang sama: [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) lalu melaporkan jumlah `CX`, dan [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) menerima fungsi filter untuk mengukur depth dua-qubit. Perhatikan bahwa `reps` ini adalah kedalaman dekomposisi, tidak ada hubungannya dengan jumlah langkah Trotter yang diambil product formula, yang di bagian selanjutnya panduan ini juga disebut `reps`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twenty-six `CX` gates in twenty-three layers, so almost nothing runs in parallel. Drawing the circuit shows why:\n"
msgstr "Dua puluh enam gate `CX` dalam dua puluh tiga layer, jadi hampir tidak ada yang berjalan paralel. Menggambar circuit-nya menunjukkan alasannya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every term has been compiled in isolation: a basis change, a `CX` ladder down to a single rotation, then the ladder is undone. The weight-1 flow set is free; its terms are lone rotations with no ladder around them, but each weight-3 term pays for four `CX`gates, and because the ladders are emitted sequentially, nothing overlaps.\n"
msgstr "Setiap suku dikompilasi secara terpisah: perubahan basis, tangga `CX` turun ke satu rotasi, lalu tangganya dibatalkan. Flow set berbobot 1 itu gratis; suku-sukunya hanya rotasi tunggal tanpa tangga di sekitarnya, tetapi setiap suku berbobot 3 membayar empat gate `CX`, dan karena tangga-tangganya dihasilkan secara berurutan, tidak ada yang tumpang tindih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the grouping survives the whole pipeline (three flow sets, three mapped [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)s) and still buys almost nothing. The fermionic Trotterization of step 5 did its job; what wastes it is the *qubit-side* formula. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receives a set of terms it happens to be told nothing about, and compiles each in isolation. It cannot know they mutually commute, so it serializes what could share a basis change.\n"
msgstr "Jadi pengelompokan bertahan sepanjang pipeline (tiga flow set, tiga [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) yang dipetakan) dan tetap hampir tidak memberi keuntungan. Trotterisasi fermionik di langkah 5 sudah menjalankan tugasnya; yang menyia-nyiakannya adalah formula di sisi *qubit*. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) menerima sekumpulan suku tanpa diberi tahu apa-apa tentangnya, dan mengompilasi masing-masing secara terpisah. Ia tidak bisa tahu bahwa suku-suku itu saling komut, jadi ia menyerialkan apa yang sebenarnya bisa berbagi satu perubahan basis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the gap this encoding exists to close: two product formulas are at work, and only the fermionic one has been given the structure so far. The next step supplies a qubit-side synthesis that exploits it too.\n"
msgstr "Itulah celah yang ingin ditutup encoding ini: ada dua product formula yang bekerja, dan sejauh ini hanya yang fermionik yang diberi tahu strukturnya. Langkah berikutnya menyediakan sintesis di sisi qubit yang juga memanfaatkannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. A flow-set-aware synthesis {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "7. Sintesis yang sadar flow set {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recovering the advantage means telling the qubit-side synthesis about the structure. This is Section IV C of Ref. <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): because all terms of a flow set commute, they can be simultaneously diagonalized by a single Clifford circuit, rotated in one shared basis and rotated back, instead of once per term.\n"
msgstr "Memulihkan keuntungan berarti memberi tahu sintesis di sisi qubit tentang strukturnya. Ini adalah Bagian IV C dari Ref. <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): karena semua suku dalam satu flow set saling komut, suku-suku itu bisa didiagonalisasi sekaligus oleh satu circuit Clifford, dirotasi dalam satu basis bersama lalu dirotasi balik, bukan sekali per suku.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this encoding, the Clifford is simple. Conjugating by a chain of `CZ` gates on nearest neighbors maps\n"
msgstr "Untuk encoding ini, Clifford-nya sederhana. Melakukan konjugasi dengan rantai gate `CZ` pada tetangga terdekat memetakan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "simultaneously for every $j$. One `CZ` chain turns the entire weight-3 (west) flow set into a layer of independent single-qubit $X$ rotations. The [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) interface only requests a [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize) method, which is all this class implements. It carries no number of Trotter steps, because it receives one flow set at a time and so cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. That subdivision belongs a level up, in fermionic space, where an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") sees all of them at once (see [step 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"
msgstr "secara bersamaan untuk setiap $j$. Satu rantai `CZ` mengubah seluruh flow set berbobot 3 (west) menjadi satu layer rotasi $X$ satu-qubit yang independen. Antarmuka [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) hanya meminta metode [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize), dan hanya itu yang diimplementasikan kelas ini. Kelas ini tidak membawa jumlah langkah Trotter, karena ia menerima satu flow set pada satu waktu sehingga tidak bisa membagi evolusi ke seluruh set. Pembagian itu ada satu level di atas, di ruang fermionik, tempat sebuah [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") melihat semuanya sekaligus (lihat [langkah 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Two details are easy to miss. A custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) must expose a `preserve_order` attribute, which the high-level-synthesis pass reads.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Dua detail gampang terlewat. Sebuah [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) kustom harus menyediakan atribut `preserve_order`, yang dibaca oleh pass high-level-synthesis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Both helpers emit their gates in explicit layers rather than in term order, because [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) schedules gates *as soon as possible, in the order they were added*. Since all the gates within one of these sets commute, the order is free to choose. A term-by-term synthesis chooses the order badly. Emitting the overlapping `CZ` chain sequentially reports a depth that grows with the qubit count rather than the constant `2` the hardware could achieve.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kedua helper menghasilkan gate-nya dalam layer eksplisit, bukan sesuai urutan suku, karena [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) menjadwalkan gate *secepat mungkin, sesuai urutan penambahannya*. Karena semua gate dalam satu set ini saling komut, urutannya bebas dipilih. Sintesis suku demi suku memilih urutan yang buruk. Menghasilkan rantai `CZ` yang tumpang tindih secara berurutan akan melaporkan depth yang bertambah seiring jumlah qubit, bukan `2` konstan yang bisa dicapai hardware.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is why the synthesis above carries no number of Trotter steps. It receives one flow set per gate, so a repetition inside it would repeat *within* a set rather than cycling between them:\n"
msgstr "  Inilah sebabnya sintesis di atas tidak membawa jumlah langkah Trotter. Ia menerima satu flow set per gate, sehingga pengulangan di dalamnya akan mengulang *di dalam* satu set, bukan berputar di antara set-set itu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The first form buys nothing: consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/2) A(t/2)` is just `A(t)` and the error stays at its one-step value however many steps are asked for.\n"
msgstr "  Bentuk pertama tidak memberi apa-apa: eksponensial berurutan dari operator yang sama saling komut, jadi `A(t/2) A(t/2)` sama saja dengan `A(t)` dan errornya tetap di nilai satu langkah, berapa pun langkah yang diminta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The step count therefore belongs to the fermionic [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") of [step 5](#flowsets-build), which reads the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") and can interleave them. That division of labor is the point: the fermionic formula decides *how many steps* and *in what order*, and this class decides *how cheaply* each resulting set is realized.\n"
msgstr "  Jumlah langkah karena itu milik [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") fermionik dari [langkah 5](#flowsets-build), yang membaca [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") dan bisa menyisipkannya bergantian. Pembagian tugas itulah intinya: formula fermionik menentukan *berapa langkah* dan *dalam urutan apa*, sedangkan kelas ini menentukan *seberapa murah* tiap set diwujudkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To select the order, pass it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), which is the argument `flow_set_pass_manager` takes. Nothing else about the pipeline (or the fermionic circuit it runs on) changes:\n"
msgstr "Untuk memilih urutannya, berikan ke [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), yang merupakan argumen yang diterima `flow_set_pass_manager`. Tidak ada hal lain dari pipeline (atau fermionic circuit tempat ia berjalan) yang berubah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From depth 23 with 26 `CX` gates down to depth 12 with 22 `CX` gates. Note that this is fewer entangling gates and nearly half the depth. Comparing the two pictures, the difference is not that the gates are cheaper but that they *stack*. The serial ladders are gone; entangling gates now sit above one another in shared layers because the whole west flow set is rotated in a single shared basis and the interaction is emitted in layers of disjoint pairs.\n"
msgstr "Dari depth 23 dengan 26 gate `CX` turun ke depth 12 dengan 22 gate `CX`. Perhatikan bahwa ini berarti gate entangling lebih sedikit dan depth hampir setengahnya. Kalau membandingkan kedua gambar, bedanya bukan karena gate-nya lebih murah, tetapi karena gate-nya *bertumpuk*. Tangga serial sudah hilang; gate entangling sekarang berada di atas satu sama lain dalam layer bersama karena seluruh flow set west dirotasi dalam satu basis bersama dan interaksinya dihasilkan dalam layer pasangan yang saling lepas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` pattern-matches *absolute* qubit indices, which is safe here only because every flow set of this Hamiltonian spans the whole register. A fermionic product formula narrows each factor to the modes it actually touches, so a grouping whose sets covered only part of the chain would arrive relabeled and the patterns above would not match.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` melakukan pencocokan pola pada indeks qubit *absolut*, yang aman di sini hanya karena setiap flow set dari Hamiltonian ini mencakup seluruh register. Product formula fermionik mempersempit tiap faktor ke mode yang benar-benar disentuhnya, jadi pengelompokan yang set-setnya hanya mencakup sebagian rantai akan datang dengan label yang sudah dinomori ulang dan pola di atas tidak akan cocok.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both drawings show the circuit after `decompose(reps=6)`, which rewrites everything into the `U` and `CX` basis, so the `CZ`, `Rx`, and `Rzz` gates emitted by `FlowSetSynthesis` are not visible as such. That is deliberate: it puts both circuits in the same basis, which is the only way the two-qubit counts and depths above are comparable. It is the *layer structure* that is notable in these figures, not the gate labels.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua gambar menunjukkan circuit setelah `decompose(reps=6)`, yang menulis ulang semuanya ke basis `U` dan `CX`, sehingga gate `CZ`, `Rx`, dan `Rzz` yang dihasilkan oleh `FlowSetSynthesis` tidak terlihat sebagai gate-gate itu. Ini disengaja: cara ini menempatkan kedua circuit dalam basis yang sama, satu-satunya cara agar jumlah dan depth dua-qubit di atas bisa dibandingkan. Yang patut diperhatikan dalam gambar-gambar ini adalah *struktur layer*-nya, bukan label gate-nya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"constant-depth-at-scale\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-scaling\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Constant depth at scale {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"
msgstr "8. Depth konstan pada skala besar {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interesting question is not the count at four modes but how it *scales*. The two `CZ` brickwork layers do not grow with the chain length, so the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step should be constant. Measuring it directly on the full Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian, well past what could be simulated by brute force:\n"
msgstr "Pertanyaan menariknya bukan jumlah di empat mode, tetapi bagaimana ia *berskala*. Dua layer brickwork `CZ` tidak bertambah seiring panjang rantai, jadi depth dua-qubit satu langkah Trotter seharusnya konstan. Mengukurnya langsung pada Hamiltonian Fermi-Hubbard penuh, jauh melampaui apa yang bisa disimulasikan dengan brute force:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit **depth stays at 12** from four modes to 100, while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) grows linearly to 407. The flow sets let it parallelize a little *within* the pipeline, but each set is still Trotterized term by term, so the growth is only slowed, not removed:\n"
msgstr "**Depth dua-qubit tetap 12** dari empat mode sampai 100, sedangkan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) tumbuh linear sampai 407. Flow set membuatnya bisa sedikit diparalelkan *di dalam* pipeline, tetapi tiap set tetap di-Trotterisasi suku demi suku, jadi pertumbuhannya hanya diperlambat, bukan dihilangkan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gate count grows linearly under both (there are $O(N)$ terms to apply, and that is unavoidable), but the flow-set synthesis applies them in a constant number of parallel layers. This is the constant-depth result of Ref. <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"
msgstr "Jumlah gate tumbuh linear pada keduanya (ada $O(N)$ suku yang harus diterapkan, dan itu tak terhindarkan), tetapi sintesis flow set menerapkannya dalam jumlah layer paralel yang konstan. Inilah hasil depth konstan dari Ref. <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The depth 12 splits across the three flow sets as 0 + 4 + 8, at every chain length. The east flow set contributes **zero**; it is bare `Rx` rotations. The west flow set costs 4, from the two `CZ` brickwork layers going in and the two coming out; dropping the interaction leaves a two-qubit depth of **four** at any chain length. The remaining **eight** is the interaction whose `Rzz` terms act on both nearest and next-nearest neighbors and so need four disjoint layers, each costing two `CX`gates. Four is optimal here: every interior qubit carries four `Rzz` gates (two to each neighbor and two to each next-nearest one) and can only take part in one at a time, so no schedule can do better.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Depth 12 terbagi ke tiga flow set sebagai 0 + 4 + 8, pada setiap panjang rantai. Flow set east menyumbang **nol**; isinya hanya rotasi `Rx` murni. Flow set west berbiaya 4, dari dua layer brickwork `CZ` yang masuk dan dua yang keluar; kalau interaksinya dibuang, depth dua-qubit-nya **empat** pada panjang rantai berapa pun. Sisa **delapan** adalah interaksi yang suku `Rzz`-nya bekerja pada tetangga terdekat maupun tetangga terdekat kedua sehingga butuh empat layer yang saling lepas, masing-masing berbiaya dua gate `CX`. Empat itu optimal di sini: setiap qubit interior membawa empat gate `Rzz` (dua ke tiap tetangga dan dua ke tiap tetangga kedua) dan hanya bisa ikut serta dalam satu pada satu waktu, jadi tidak ada jadwal yang bisa lebih baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Two thirds of the depth is the interaction, which shows that this encoding excels at the hopping, and thus at the dynamics of a free-fermion chain. However, note that the interaction does not commute with the hopping. Leaving it out is *not* an approximation to Fermi-Hubbard but a different model. Where the balance falls for a given problem is worth exploring.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dua pertiga depth adalah interaksi, yang menunjukkan bahwa encoding ini unggul pada hopping, dan karena itu pada dinamika rantai fermion bebas. Namun, perhatikan bahwa interaksi tidak komut dengan hopping. Membuangnya *bukan* aproksimasi untuk Fermi-Hubbard, melainkan model yang berbeda. Di mana keseimbangannya jatuh untuk suatu masalah patut dieksplorasi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"check-the-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-check-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Check the dynamics {#9-check-the-dynamics}"
msgstr "9. Periksa dinamikanya {#9-check-the-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under the domain-wall map, an occupation pattern becomes a cumulative-parity string, so the initial state is prepared differently than under Jordan-Wigner. This is an easily overlooked practical consequence of delocalizing the parity. The helper from step 4 gives the right label:\n"
msgstr "Di bawah peta domain-wall, pola okupansi menjadi string paritas kumulatif, jadi state awalnya disiapkan secara berbeda dari di Jordan-Wigner. Ini konsekuensi praktis yang mudah terlewat dari delokalisasi paritas. Helper dari langkah 4 memberikan label yang benar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the state prepared, two questions remain, and they are best asked separately: does the flow-set synthesis compute the *right* thing, and does it compute it more *cheaply*?\n"
msgstr "Dengan state yang sudah disiapkan, tersisa dua pertanyaan, dan paling baik ditanyakan terpisah: apakah sintesis flow set menghitung hal yang *benar*, dan apakah ia menghitungnya dengan lebih *murah*?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Take correctness first. `FlowSetSynthesis` and Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receive the same encoded flow sets from the same fermionic Trotterization, so they must realize the same unitary up to a global phase. The custom Cliffords reorganize the work; they do not change the result. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Mari mulai dari kebenaran. `FlowSetSynthesis` dan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) milik Qiskit menerima flow set ter-encode yang sama dari Trotterisasi fermionik yang sama, jadi keduanya harus mewujudkan unitari yang sama hingga fase global. Clifford kustom hanya menata ulang pekerjaannya; hasilnya tidak berubah. Statevector acak mendeteksi ketidaksesuaian apa pun jauh lebih murah daripada membangun unitari penuh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the *same* phase across several random states is what closes the gap. Checking more than one [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") matters too, since it confirms the agreement survives the interleaving of the flow sets rather than holding only for a single sweep.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua bagian dari pemeriksaan itu penting. Overlap bermodulus satu pada satu state itu perlu tetapi belum cukup: sintesis yang salah di fase yang bergantung pada state tetap akan terlihat. Mensyaratkan fase yang *sama* di beberapa state acak itulah yang menutup celahnya. Memeriksa lebih dari satu [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") juga penting, karena itu memastikan kesesuaiannya bertahan melewati penyisipan flow set, bukan hanya berlaku untuk satu sapuan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the choice of qubit-side synthesis is free of consequence for accuracy, which is what makes a cost comparison meaningful. The remaining question is what the encoding as a whole buys against the obvious alternative: plain Jordan-Wigner on `num_sites` qubits, with no ancilla and no custom Cliffords. Both the encoding and the qubit-side synthesis differ between the two columns, but the check above showed the latter cannot affect the result, so what the fidelities test is the encoding. Both pipelines also start from the *same* fermionic Trotterization, so any difference in fidelity would indicate a bug rather than a trade-off. The two columns are the *encodings*, flow-set against Jordan-Wigner:\n"
msgstr "Jadi pilihan sintesis di sisi qubit tidak berpengaruh pada akurasi, dan itulah yang membuat perbandingan biaya bermakna. Pertanyaan yang tersisa adalah apa yang didapat dari encoding secara keseluruhan dibanding alternatif yang jelas: Jordan-Wigner biasa pada `num_sites` qubit, tanpa ancilla dan tanpa Clifford kustom. Baik encoding maupun sintesis di sisi qubit berbeda di antara kedua kolom, tetapi pemeriksaan di atas menunjukkan yang terakhir tidak bisa memengaruhi hasil, jadi yang diuji fidelity itu adalah encoding-nya. Kedua pipeline juga mulai dari Trotterisasi fermionik yang *sama*, jadi perbedaan fidelity apa pun akan menandakan bug, bukan trade-off. Kedua kolom itu adalah *encoding*, flow-set melawan Jordan-Wigner:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the fidelity column first: identical, to every printed digit, in two different Hilbert spaces under two different encodings. That is the fermionic Trotterization showing through. The approximation was fixed in step 5, before either encoding was chosen, so both circuits carry exactly the error of a first-order formula over three flow sets, and it falls roughly four-fold per doubling of the step count.\n"
msgstr "Baca dulu kolom fidelity: identik, sampai setiap digit yang dicetak, di dua ruang Hilbert berbeda dengan dua encoding berbeda. Itulah Trotterisasi fermionik yang terlihat. Aproksimasinya ditetapkan di langkah 5, sebelum salah satu encoding dipilih, jadi kedua circuit membawa error yang persis sama dari formula orde pertama atas tiga flow set, dan error itu turun sekitar empat kali lipat untuk setiap penggandaan jumlah langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the encodings do differ in is cost, and the trade is worth stating plainly. The flow set spends **more** entangling gates: 22 against 18 at one step. The ancilla is not the reason, since it carries no two-qubit gate of its own. The reason is the interaction, exactly as [step 3](#flowsets-encoding) warned: delocalizing the parity turns three nearest-neighbor `ZZ` terms into seven spanning nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors, and each costs two `CX` gates. That is the price paid for making the hopping cheap.\n"
msgstr "Yang berbeda antara kedua encoding adalah biayanya, dan trade-off-nya layak dinyatakan terus terang. Flow set mengeluarkan gate entangling **lebih banyak**: 22 lawan 18 pada satu langkah. Ancilla bukan penyebabnya, karena ia tidak membawa gate dua-qubit sendiri. Penyebabnya adalah interaksi, persis seperti yang diperingatkan [langkah 3](#flowsets-encoding): delokalisasi paritas mengubah tiga suku `ZZ` tetangga terdekat menjadi tujuh suku yang mencakup tetangga terdekat *dan* tetangga terdekat kedua, dan masing-masing berbiaya dua gate `CX`. Itulah harga yang dibayar agar hopping jadi murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It also wins only narrowly on depth at this size (12 against 14), because four modes is too small for the asymptotics to show. The point is the *scaling* measured in [step 8](#flowsets-scaling): that depth of 12 is constant, while the Jordan-Wigner depth grows with the chain. At 14 modes it is already 12 against 34.\n"
msgstr "Keunggulan di depth juga hanya tipis pada ukuran ini (12 lawan 14), karena empat mode terlalu kecil untuk memperlihatkan asimtotiknya. Intinya ada pada *skala* yang diukur di [langkah 8](#flowsets-scaling): depth 12 itu konstan, sementara depth Jordan-Wigner tumbuh seiring rantai. Pada 14 mode sudah 12 lawan 34.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) calls above are essential, for two independent reasons.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Peringatan\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Panggilan [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) di atas itu penting, karena dua alasan yang independen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) and [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) use a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s *exact* definition, bypassing a custom qubit-side synthesis. Verifying against an un-decomposed circuit reports perfect fidelity even for a deliberately wrong synthesis.\n"
msgstr "  [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) dan [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) memakai definisi *eksak* dari sebuah [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), melewati sintesis kustom di sisi qubit. Memverifikasi terhadap circuit yang tidak didekomposisi akan melaporkan fidelity sempurna bahkan untuk sintesis yang sengaja dibuat salah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The same applies one level up, to the fermionic synthesis. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed goes to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which maps it without consulting `Evolution.synthesis` at all, so [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") would silently have no effect. `trotter_steps` from step 5 performs that decomposition; a pipeline that sets the method with [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") gets the same expansion from the pass instead.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Hal yang sama berlaku satu level di atas, untuk sintesis fermionik. Sebuah gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang tidak pernah didekomposisi masuk utuh ke tahap fermion-ke-qubit, yang memetakannya tanpa merujuk `Evolution.synthesis` sama sekali, sehingga [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") diam-diam tidak akan berpengaruh. `trotter_steps` dari langkah 5 melakukan dekomposisi itu; pipeline yang menetapkan metodenya dengan [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") mendapat ekspansi yang sama dari pass tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a final cross-check, the site densities $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ computed in the encoded space must reproduce the Jordan-Wigner result. This check is about the *encoding*, not the circuit, so no Trotter approximation enters it. Both time evolutions are computed exactly, by matrix exponentiation of the respective Hamiltonians. Any discrepancy would therefore point at the encoding rather than a product formula:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai pemeriksaan silang terakhir, densitas site $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ yang dihitung di ruang ter-encode harus mereproduksi hasil Jordan-Wigner. Pemeriksaan ini menyangkut *encoding*, bukan circuit, jadi tidak ada aproksimasi Trotter yang masuk. Kedua evolusi waktu dihitung secara eksak, dengan eksponensiasi matriks dari masing-masing Hamiltonian. Ketidaksesuaian apa pun karena itu akan menunjuk ke encoding, bukan ke product formula:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The densities agree to ten decimal places.\n"
msgstr "Densitasnya cocok sampai sepuluh angka desimal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Yang perlu dibawa pulang {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping.** Flow sets are defined on the directed fermionic interaction graph, so the grouping is chosen while problem structure is still available. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute carries it into the circuit, where a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) turns it into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per flow set.\n"
msgstr "**Kelompokkan sebelum memetakan.** Flow set didefinisikan pada graf interaksi fermionik berarah, jadi pengelompokan dipilih selagi struktur masalah masih tersedia. Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") membawanya ke dalam circuit, tempat satu [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) mengubahnya menjadi satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ancillas buy structure.** Spending one extra qubit turns an entire flow set into weight-1 Paulis, whose evolution needs no entangling gates. Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) observes this trade-off generally. Larger qubit-to-fermion ratios admit shallower evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Ancilla membeli struktur.** Mengeluarkan satu qubit tambahan mengubah seluruh flow set menjadi Pauli berbobot 1, yang evolusinya tidak butuh gate entangling. Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) mengamati trade-off ini secara umum. Rasio qubit-ke-fermion yang lebih besar memungkinkan circuit evolusi yang lebih dangkal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A custom encoding is one function.** Map a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") do the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Encoding kustom itu satu fungsi.** Petakan satu operator transfer umum ke satu string Pauli; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") mengerjakan sisanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The mapping and the grouping alone are not enough.** Splitting the evolution per flow set only slowed the linear growth in depth; a term-by-term synthesis of each set still threw away the fact that its terms commute. Only supplying a flow-set-aware [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) made the depth constant. Custom encodings, grouping, and custom synthesis are complementary: all three are needed.\n"
msgstr "**Pemetaan dan pengelompokan saja tidak cukup.** Memecah evolusi per flow set hanya memperlambat pertumbuhan linear depth; sintesis suku demi suku untuk tiap set tetap membuang fakta bahwa suku-sukunya saling komut. Hanya dengan menyediakan [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) yang sadar flow set, depth menjadi konstan. Encoding kustom, pengelompokan, dan sintesis kustom saling melengkapi: ketiganya dibutuhkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two product formulas, two jobs.** [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") fixes the approximation in fermionic space, where the grouping is still visible, so it alone sets the Trotter error and the step count. The qubit-side [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) then decides only how cheaply each set is realized: step 9 confirms both choices give the same unitary. Separating the two is what lets the accuracy and the cost be tuned independently. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"
msgstr "**Dua product formula, dua tugas.** [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") menetapkan aproksimasi di ruang fermionik, tempat pengelompokan masih terlihat, jadi hanya ia yang menentukan error Trotter dan jumlah langkah. [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) di sisi qubit lalu hanya menentukan seberapa murah tiap set diwujudkan: langkah 9 mengonfirmasi bahwa kedua pilihan memberi unitari yang sama. Memisahkan keduanya membuat akurasi dan biaya bisa diatur secara independen. Lihat [Sintesis gate Evolution di ruang fermionik](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify it.** An encoding that satisfies the commutation relations might still represent a different Hamiltonian if a prefactor or sign is off. Checking an intertwining relation (or, more cheaply, the spectrum) catches this.\n"
msgstr "**Verifikasi.** Encoding yang memenuhi relasi komutasi mungkin tetap merepresentasikan Hamiltonian yang berbeda kalau ada prefaktor atau tanda yang meleset. Memeriksa relasi intertwining (atau, yang lebih murah, spektrumnya) akan menangkap hal ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `FlowSetSynthesis` above is deliberately written for *this* encoding on a 1D chain. It pattern-matches the specific Pauli labels the encoding produces and raises on anything else, rather than silently falling back to a generic product formula. A general implementation has two halves. Reading the flow-set structure from the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") is what a [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") for an evolution already does. Deriving the diagonalizing Clifford from the stabilizer group, as described in Section IV C of Ref.   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), is the half that remains encoding specific.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` di atas sengaja ditulis untuk encoding *ini* pada rantai 1D. Ia mencocokkan pola label Pauli spesifik yang dihasilkan encoding dan memunculkan error untuk yang lain, bukan diam-diam kembali ke product formula generik. Implementasi umum punya dua bagian. Membaca struktur flow set dari [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") milik operator adalah hal yang sudah dilakukan sebuah [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") untuk sebuah evolusi. Menurunkan Clifford yang mendiagonalisasi dari grup stabilizer, seperti dijelaskan di Bagian IV C Ref.   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), adalah bagian yang tetap spesifik untuk encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Also, delocalizing the parity makes the interaction term $n_j n_{j+1}$ weight-2 rather than diagonal in single qubits, which is the counterpart cost to the cheaper hopping terms.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Selain itu, delokalisasi paritas membuat suku interaksi $n_j n_{j+1}$ berbobot 2, bukan diagonal pada qubit tunggal, yang merupakan biaya pasangan dari suku hopping yang lebih murah.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next: two dimensions {#next-two-dimensions}"
msgstr "Berikutnya: dua dimensi {#next-two-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything above is one-dimensional, and deliberately so. On a chain, the flow sets are just the two arrow orientations, and the encoding needs a single ancilla. Neither simplification survives in two dimensions, which is where local encodings are needed.\n"
msgstr "Semua di atas bersifat satu dimensi, dan memang disengaja. Pada sebuah rantai, flow set hanyalah dua orientasi panah, dan encoding-nya butuh satu ancilla saja. Kedua penyederhanaan itu tidak bertahan di dua dimensi, tempat encoding lokal dibutuhkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a planar lattice, a flow set is a directed path (or a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths) through the interaction graph, and finding a small set of such paths that covers every edge becomes a combinatorial problem in its own right, rather than a two-line classification. The encodings also change character; instead of a single ancilla for the whole chain, they add one per lattice site or cell. Verstraete-Cirac pairs every fermionic site with its own auxiliary qubit, a qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$, while Derby-Klassen places one at the center of each odd plaquette, for a ratio of $3/2$. The register layout then has genuine two-dimensional structure, and the stabilizer group that must be projected onto is no longer trivial. The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a *subspace*, which changes both state preparation and the verification recipe from [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
msgstr "Pada kisi planar, sebuah flow set adalah lintasan berarah (atau gabungan lintasan berarah yang saling lepas titik-sudutnya) melalui graf interaksi, dan mencari himpunan kecil lintasan semacam itu yang menutupi setiap sisi menjadi masalah kombinatorial tersendiri, bukan klasifikasi dua baris. Encoding-nya juga berubah karakter; alih-alih satu ancilla untuk seluruh rantai, mereka menambah satu per site atau sel kisi. Verstraete-Cirac memasangkan setiap site fermionik dengan qubit bantu miliknya sendiri, rasio qubit-ke-mode sebesar $2$, sedangkan Derby-Klassen menempatkan satu di pusat setiap plaquette ganjil, dengan rasio $3/2$. Tata letak register lalu punya struktur dua dimensi yang sesungguhnya, dan grup stabilizer yang harus diproyeksikan tidak lagi trivial. Hamiltonian ter-encode hanya faithful pada sebuah *subruang*, yang mengubah persiapan state maupun resep verifikasi dari [langkah 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pieces this guide builds are the ones that carry over: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for a register whose size differs from the mode count, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding itself, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") for wiring it into the transpiler, and a custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) for making the flow-set structure pay off. Only the encoding and the flow-set decomposition are different.\n"
msgstr "Bagian-bagian yang dibangun panduan ini adalah yang terbawa ke sana: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") untuk register yang ukurannya berbeda dari jumlah mode, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") untuk encoding itu sendiri, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") untuk menyambungkannya ke transpiler, dan [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) kustom agar struktur flow set membuahkan hasil. Hanya encoding dan dekomposisi flow set yang berbeda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [2D flow-set guide](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) picks up here, working through the Verstraete-Cirac encoding on a square lattice: four flow sets, a depth-2 Clifford for each, and the stabilizer projection the verification then needs.\n"
msgstr "[Panduan flow set 2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) melanjutkan dari sini, mengerjakan encoding Verstraete-Cirac pada kisi persegi: empat flow set, Clifford berdepth 2 untuk masing-masing, dan proyeksi stabilizer yang kemudian dibutuhkan verifikasi.\n"

